WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.495
Critical thinking improves the quality of questions, evidence evaluation, assumptions, reasoning, and decisions.

2
00:00:07.495 --> 00:00:11.843
It is not about rejecting every claim or trying to win every argument.

3
00:00:11.843 --> 00:00:19.113
It is about making conclusions more reliable by examining how they were formed and how strongly they are supported.

4
00:00:19.113 --> 00:00:21.662
The first habit is to identify the claim.

5
00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:26.909
Separate facts, interpretations, opinions, predictions, and recommendations.

6
00:00:26.909 --> 00:00:34.104
Ask what would need to be true, what evidence is relevant, whether the evidence is sufficient, and what is missing.

7
00:00:34.104 --> 00:00:39.876
Strong conclusions require support that fits the importance and consequence of the claim.

8
00:00:39.876 --> 00:00:43.399
The second habit is to examine assumptions and framing.

9
00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:53.517
Ask what is being taken for granted, how the problem has been defined, what context matters, and whether incentives or stakeholders change the interpretation.

10
00:00:53.517 --> 00:01:01.088
Framing shapes which evidence is noticed and which solutions appear reasonable, so it deserves deliberate attention.

11
00:01:01.088 --> 00:01:03.636
The third habit is to inspect reasoning.

12
00:01:03.636 --> 00:01:15.254
Look at premises and conclusions, cause and effect, correlation and causation, necessary and sufficient conditions, false dilemmas, circular reasoning, and overgeneralization.

13
00:01:15.254 --> 00:01:25.823
Then account for predictable thinking traps such as confirmation bias, anchoring, availability, overconfidence, sunk cost, motivated reasoning, and groupthink.

14
00:01:25.823 --> 00:01:31.369
The final habit is to communicate uncertainty honestly and review decisions over time.

15
00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:40.664
Evaluate sources, use AI-generated material critically, make tradeoffs visible, document reasoning, and welcome constructive disagreement.

16
00:01:40.664 --> 00:01:49.883
The goal is practical judgment: better conclusions, better decisions, fewer avoidable errors, and more reliable action under real conditions.
